<section id="word-reading-order">
					<section>
						<h1>Reading order</h1>

					</section>

					<section>
						<h2>Don't use textboxes (or any floating elements) </h2>
						<p>As alternative, style your text with a border. </p>
					</section>

					<section>
						<h2>Be careful when using tables for layout </h2>
						<ul>
							<li>The reading order is line by line</li>
							<li>If you need a column layout use layout > columns</li>
						</ul>
					</section>
					<section>
						<p>Reading order problems are often caused by a complex layout. If layout is complex, Word is not the right tool to make an accessible PDF document. Adobe Indesign is better. </p>
					</section>

				</section>
